1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,219
See how RF warehouse screens are configured in Quark's
WebRF Studio, using receiving screens as the example.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:18,268
The new screen dialog offers different screen types. The
editor then brings together the screen list, a visual
preview, and configuration properties.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,553
Switch between handheld and forklift display layouts. The
main menu preview shows how warehouse operations are
presented on each screen format.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,533
Open the ASN Receipt screen and add example widgets. Each
added item appears in the preview and in the widget list.

5
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,856
Select a choice field to inspect its properties. Its
identifier, label, type, placement, and input settings are
shown together in the property panel.

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,135
Add number and lookup fields to the screen. Select each
widget to inspect its individual input settings in the
properties panel.

7
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,044
A date widget adds a date entry to the preview. Selecting
it exposes the settings for that specific field.

8
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:45,814
Remove the temporary example fields and return to the ASN
input. The preview follows the changes made in the
designer.

9
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:07,251
Screen settings bring together the title, operator prompt,
configured submit action, and navigation links. Version
information distinguishes published definitions from work
in a draft.

10
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:21,409
The logic panel exposes configured response handling. Move
through the connected receiving screens to inspect their
settings and function keys.

11
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:53,565
Receive Line shows quantity, unit of measure, lot, expiry,
destination location, and pallet identification. Lot and
expiry are marked as conditional fields.

12
00:02:54,500 --> 00:03:02,976
Select the destination location field to review required
entry, uppercase handling, and the order in which its
value is sent.

13
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:12,008
Switch between the light and dark previews to inspect the
same receiving screen in both themes.

14
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:23,838
This walkthrough brings screen layout, field properties,
and navigation settings together in Quark’s RF screen
designer.
